\newlabel{fig:bottleneck}{{1}{2}{\textbf {Left:} almost all current error is the exact Bayesian risk conditioned on the available measurements. \textbf {Right:} analytic weighted posterior risk for sequential point measurements, with and without observation noise. The grey curve is the more optimistic spectral lower bound obtained if one were allowed arbitrary noiseless rank-$B$ linear measurements rather than point sensors. The current budget $B=8$ is marked vertically}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {2}The primary bottleneck is the measurement budget}{3}{section.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {3}The reported design loss was not a global reconstruction loss}{3}{section.3}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces A representative held-out function. More recurrent computation aligns the loop with the exact GP mean but cannot recover the unobserved left boundary. Doubling the budget and optimizing global coverage removes the dominant uncertainty and produces a genuinely accurate reconstruction.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
